WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.380
Light an oat seedling from one side, and its shoot bends toward the lamp.

2
00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:10.140
The tip is where the light is mainly sensed.

3
00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:12.460
But the bend forms lower down.

4
00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:14.820
What carries the message between them?

5
00:00:15.733 --> 00:00:20.353
Charles Darwin and his son Francis lit canary grass seedlings from one side.

6
00:00:21.233 --> 00:00:25.413
An opaque cap over the tip greatly reduced bending, even though the lower part was

7
00:00:25.413 --> 00:00:29.713
still lit. A transparent glass tube over the tip did not stop it.

8
00:00:30.553 --> 00:00:34.493
Light is sensed mainly near the tip, and something passes down to where the bending

9
00:00:34.493 --> 00:00:35.493
happens.

10
00:00:35.967 --> 00:00:41.067
Peter Boysen-Jensen worked with oat coleoptiles, the sheath over the first leaf of a

11
00:00:41.067 --> 00:00:44.627
grass seedling. He cut off tips and set them back in place.

12
00:00:45.447 --> 00:00:49.467
The coleoptile still bent below the cut, so the influence crossed a wound.

13
00:00:50.307 --> 00:00:52.767
Then he slid mica into a cut below the tip.

14
00:00:53.747 --> 00:00:55.607
Dissolved chemicals cannot cross mica.

15
00:00:56.627 --> 00:00:58.687
Mica on the lit side left bending intact.

16
00:00:59.807 --> 00:01:01.427
Mica on the shaded side blocked it.

17
00:01:02.167 --> 00:01:05.047
He concluded that the signal runs down the shaded side.

18
00:01:06.017 --> 00:01:08.157
Frits Went took the signal out of the plant.

19
00:01:08.997 --> 00:01:13.777
He stood cut tips of dark-grown oat coleoptiles on small blocks of agar, then

20
00:01:13.777 --> 00:01:18.637
removed the tips. In the dark, he set a block on one side of a decapitated

21
00:01:18.637 --> 00:01:22.357
coleoptile. The coleoptile curved away from the block.

22
00:01:23.437 --> 00:01:24.657
Plain agar caused no curve.

23
00:01:25.477 --> 00:01:29.877
A substance from the tips had entered the agar and sped elongation beneath it.

24
00:01:30.697 --> 00:01:32.597
Auxin was identified later, by others.

25
00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:35.510
Why does the shaded side get more?

26
00:01:36.290 --> 00:01:40.830
The Cholodny-Went hypothesis says that light from one side moves auxin sideways,

27
00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:42.430
toward the shaded flank.

28
00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:46.650
That flank elongates faster, so the shoot bends toward the light.

29
00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:52.530
In Arabidopsis hypocotyls, light changes where a carrier called PIN3 sits in the

30
00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:58.310
cell membrane. Many PIN carriers sit mainly on one face of a cell, so repositioning

31
00:01:58.310 --> 00:01:59.390
them steers auxin.

32
00:02:00.333 --> 00:02:02.393
A worked bioassay shows the logic.

33
00:02:03.333 --> 00:02:06.313
These numbers are illustrative, not from a real experiment.

34
00:02:07.213 --> 00:02:13.793
A split tip lit from one side gives 0.03 mg per L of auxin from the lit half, and

35
00:02:13.793 --> 00:02:16.273
0.06 from the shaded half.

36
00:02:17.033 --> 00:02:20.793
A tip kept in the dark gives 0.09, the same total.

37
00:02:21.813 --> 00:02:23.793
Light did not destroy auxin on the lit side.

38
00:02:24.653 --> 00:02:26.373
It moved auxin to the shaded side.

39
00:02:27.153 --> 00:02:30.893
Each flank's growth follows its auxin level, and the curve is the difference.
